GlassineOS wvkbd
================

This branch is the on-screen keyboard of GlassineOS (https://github.com/GlassineOS):
wvkbd 0.21 (https://github.com/jjsullivan5196/wvkbd) plus these changes:

  - themable keys: --stroke, --stroke-sp, --stroke-width and --gap (the shell
    passes its theme's look). The pressed-key label (--text-press, --text-press-sp)
    and --no-popup were added here for 0.16; upstream has them since, so this
    branch uses upstream's. A swiped key's label is --text's unless --text-swipe
    is given (upstream's default is white), as it was in 0.16.
  - a German QWERTZ layer ("german") with umlauts
  - long press (--hold MS, default 400, 0: off): a held key types the
    alternate printed in its corner (":" on ".", ";" on ",", symbols on the
    letters), on the full, landscape and German layers.
  - the keyboard as the input method (GlassineOS/shell spec 006), all behind
    --im: text is committed to the focused text field (zwp_input_method_v2),
    Backspace deletes through it where the field reports its text, other keys
    stay key events. The field's purpose picks the keys: number, phone and PIN
    pads, an address row (@) for email, a URL row (/ .com). Private fields
    (password, PIN, sensitive or hidden text) send nothing to the predictor and
    print nothing on stdout.
      --strip          the suggestion strip above the keys: three words, the
                       likeliest in the middle; a pen key (--pen-cmd) and a
                       hide key (--hide-cmd); holding a word asks to remove it
      --predictor CMD  the word predictor, a child process on a socket pair
                       (docs/predictor.md of GlassineOS/shell); missing, slow
                       or crashed: an empty strip, started again with backoff
      --lang LIST      the languages sent (default: the layout's)
      --notify SOCKET  focus reports to the session ("osk focus 1 PURPOSE",
                       "osk focus 0", "osk changed", "osk im")
    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glassine/predict.conf: "suggestions = off" leaves the strip
    empty and sends nothing, "handwriting = off" hides the pen key and the
    paper, "handwriting_pause = MS" (200..5000, default 800) is the pause after
    which the written text shows; read at each field focus.
  - handwriting (spec 006 FR-010..FR-013a), behind --handwriting: a writing
    paper laid over the app under the field's cursor (the input method's
    popup); the keyboard draws the ink itself and registers the paper as an
    ink area (pen brush) where the compositor has glassine-ink-v1. Each
    stroke goes to the recognizer at once; after a pause the reading is the
    field's pending text with two alternatives and a correction control above
    the ink. Writing on commits it; a picked alternative or a correction
    commits it as a lesson. A strike-through deletes the struck characters
    (on bare paper: the last word), a scratch-out discards the pending text,
    a caret inserts a space. The pen draws (pointer events: a tablet pen as
    the compositor hands it to a client without tablet support); a finger
    only taps the controls. Private fields: no paper, nothing sent.
      --handwriting CMD  the recognizer (docs/recognizer.md of
                         GlassineOS/handwriting), started on the first stroke;
                         the pen key opens the paper. Missing or crashed: ink
                         without readings, typing unaffected
      --pen-flag FILE    the session creates FILE before a show after a pen
                         tap: the paper instead of the keys, in an empty field
      --paper-height PX  the paper's height (default: the keys')
    Files: im.c (the field), predict.c (the predictor client), strip.c (the
    strip), hw.c (the recognizer client), paper.c (the paper's model and
    layout; drawn in keyboard.c), osk.c (all of them together; no Wayland,
    host-tested), textrules.h.

Without the new options, and on upstream's layers, the keyboard behaves as
upstream's.

Branches:
  glassine/0.21   what GlassineOS builds
  glassine/0.16   the release Alpine 3.22 packaged (kept)

Build: as upstream (make; needs wayland, pango, cairo, xkbcommon, scdoc).
Tests: make check (host unit tests; python3 for the stand-in predictor and
recognizer; GLASSINE_PREDICT=path adds the real predictor), make check-e2e
(headless sway in a Docker container: typing, picks, Backspace, private fields,
pads, settings, the paper with strokes from a virtual pointer;
HW_SRC=handwriting-checkout HW_MODELS=dir-with-en/recognizer.ghm adds a run with
the real recognizer).

The license is upstream's (GPL-3.0, LICENSE). Commits made with AI assistance
carry an Assisted-by: trailer. They are not submitted upstream; see the
GlassineOS contribution policy.
